title: schrodinger-hpc
message: If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hentabli
    given-names: Hamza
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9530-2815
repository-code: https://github.com/hentablihamza/schrodinger-hpc
url: https://github.com/hentablihamza/schrodinger-hpc
abstract: >
  Production-style SLURM job scripts and license-free Python helper tools for
  running Schrodinger (Glide docking and LigPrep) at scale on an academic HPC
  cluster. Includes serial and job-array Glide scripts for ultra-large virtual
  screening, protein preparation and grid generation jobs, and license-free
  tools for extracting ligands and binding-pocket residues from a PDB,
  computing a docking grid center, parsing Glide result CSVs, and summarizing
  SLURM array-job progress, with a worked EGFR (PDB 1M17) example.
keywords:
  - molecular docking
  - Glide
  - virtual screening
  - high-performance computing
  - SLURM
  - structure-based drug design
  - cheminformatics
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-24"
